Subject: detect __wasi__ as an OS, and __wasm32__ as a processor

WHAT
  src/corelib/global/qsystemdetection.h     adds a Q_OS_WASI arm.
  src/corelib/global/qprocessordetection.h  widens the Web Assembly arm from
                                            __EMSCRIPTEN__ to __wasm32__ /
                                            __wasm64__, and confines
                                            Q_PROCESSOR_WORDSIZE 8 to the
                                            targets that actually have it.

WHY
  * wasi-sdk 34-rc.2 predefines only __wasi__, __wasip2__, __wasm, __wasm32,
    __wasm32__ and __wasm__ -- no __EMSCRIPTEN__, no __linux__, no __unix__
    (verified with `clang --target=wasm32-wasip2 -dM -E -x c /dev/null`).
    qsystemdetection.h therefore falls all the way through to
    `#error "Qt has not been ported to this OS"` and not one translation unit
    compiles. Q_OS_UNIX is granted automatically by the existing fallthrough
    at the bottom of the file.

    Q_OS_WASM is deliberately NOT also defined. It would make
    qcoreapplication.cpp and qthread_p.h include qeventdispatcher_wasm_p.h,
    which is emscripten::val code that CMake is not building for us and that
    wasi-sdk cannot compile.

  * qprocessordetection.h's Web Assembly arm keys on __EMSCRIPTEN__ alone, so
    a wasi target gets neither Q_PROCESSOR_WASM nor Q_BYTE_ORDER. Qt's
    architecture config test then reports "Architecture:unknown" and
    QT_BUILD_ABI becomes "unknown-little_endian-ilp32", which is a lie any
    module that string-matches the ABI can act on.

    The existing arm also does `#define Q_PROCESSOR_WORDSIZE 8` unconditionally
    -- correct for emscripten (which models a 64-bit word even on wasm32) and
    for wasm64, wrong for wasm32-wasip2, where pointers and long are 4 bytes.
    Widening the arm without confining that line would have introduced a real
    bug, so it is now guarded.

UPSTREAM
  yes, both hunks. Small, mechanical, no policy in them: an OS macro for a
  compiler-defined target macro, and a processor arm keyed on the architecture
  rather than on one particular SDK. The WORDSIZE guard is arguably a latent
  upstream defect in its own right.

---
diff --git a/src/corelib/global/qsystemdetection.h b/src/corelib/global/qsystemdetection.h
index 0cbcef2..ac60c78 100644
--- a/src/corelib/global/qsystemdetection.h
+++ b/src/corelib/global/qsystemdetection.h
@@ -96,6 +96,13 @@
 #  define Q_OS_HPUX
 #elif defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
 #  define Q_OS_WASM
+#elif defined(__wasi__)
+// WASI is wasm with a POSIX-ish libc, NOT Emscripten. Deliberately NOT
+// Q_OS_WASM: that macro pulls in the embind event dispatcher
+// (qcoreapplication.cpp, qthread_p.h include qeventdispatcher_wasm_p.h under
+// it) and the rest of the emscripten::val code, none of which wasi-sdk can
+// compile. Q_OS_UNIX is granted automatically by the fallthrough below.
+#  define Q_OS_WASI
 #elif defined(__linux__) || defined(__linux)
 #  define Q_OS_LINUX
 #elif defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__DragonFly__) || defined(__FreeBSD_kernel__)
diff --git a/src/corelib/global/qprocessordetection.h b/src/corelib/global/qprocessordetection.h
index f7298bb..821a369 100644
--- a/src/corelib/global/qprocessordetection.h
+++ b/src/corelib/global/qprocessordetection.h
@@ -335,10 +335,19 @@
 #  define Q_BYTE_ORDER Q_BIG_ENDIAN
 
 // -- Web Assembly --
-#elif defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+// __wasm32__/__wasm64__ so that a non-Emscripten wasm target (wasi-sdk defines
+// __wasi__ and __wasm32__, never __EMSCRIPTEN__) still gets a processor and a
+// byte order; without this Qt's architecture config test reports
+// "Architecture:unknown" and QT_BUILD_ABI becomes "unknown-little_endian-ilp32".
+#elif defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) || defined(__wasm32__) || defined(__wasm64__)
 #  define Q_PROCESSOR_WASM
 #  define Q_BYTE_ORDER Q_LITTLE_ENDIAN
-#  define Q_PROCESSOR_WORDSIZE 8
+// WORDSIZE 8 is correct for emscripten (which models a 64-bit word even on
+// wasm32) and for real wasm64, but NOT for a plain 32-bit wasi target, where
+// pointers and long are 4 bytes.
+#  if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) || defined(__wasm64__)
+#    define Q_PROCESSOR_WORDSIZE 8
+#  endif
 #ifdef QT_COMPILER_SUPPORTS_SSE2
 #  define Q_PROCESSOR_X86 6   // enables SIMD support
 # define Q_PROCESSOR_X86_64 // wasm64
